			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Atomize IPC layer and inject W3C trace context\n\nDecompose monolithic IPC handler files (`AdvancedFeatures`, `DevLog`, `StatusReporter`, `WindAirCommands`, `WindServiceAdapters`) into their dedicated sibling directories, aligning with the project's strict file-per-command modularization strategy. This eliminates single-source files exceeding 30KB and prepares the `Source/IPC` layer for granular testing and independent component evolution.\n\nIntroduce `EmitWithTraceparent` to instrument outbound Tauri events with W3C `traceparent` headers. This bridge stamps `_traceparent` fields onto JSON payloads in debug builds, enabling the `Sky` UI layer to correlate frontend event handlers with backend OTLP spans. Release builds bypass this overhead via `cfg!(debug_assertions)` gating.\n\nUpdate remaining modules (`ConfigurationBridge`, `WindAdvancedSync`) to enforce explicit `::Struct` and `::Fn` qualification patterns, resolving potential symbol shadowing during the transition to the atomized architecture.",
			"SHA": "c96e22222b3ced5e16e63c598d8d953340bd7793"
		},
